# apps/web environment — copy to `.env.local` for local dev, or set these as env
# vars in the deployment host (Vercel/Netlify/etc.). Every var here is build-time
# and PUBLIC (Vite inlines VITE_* into the client bundle) — never put a secret here.
# With NONE of these set, the app still boots: mock voice + degraded no-auth mode.

# --- Voice session (LiveKit) ---
# Transport: "mock" (default, scripted/offline, no backend) or "livekit".
VITE_TRANSPORT=mock

# Backend POST /token endpoint (apps/backend). Only used when VITE_TRANSPORT=livekit.
# Local dev with the backend running: http://localhost:8000
VITE_TOKEN_ENDPOINT=

# --- Supabase auth (SIM-3; env provisioned by SIM-1/SIM-40) ---
# Both are PUBLIC (they ship in the bundle). The anon/publishable key is RLS-bounded,
# NOT a secret. NEVER put the secret / service_role key here or anywhere in apps/web
# (CI `guard-secrets` + GitHub push protection block it). Unset → degraded no-auth mode.
#
# Get both from the Supabase dashboard → Settings → API Keys.
# Live project (SIM-40): https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/ntyojhksnciusyaehxhj
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://ntyojhksnciusyaehxhj.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Turnstile CAPTCHA (FUTURE — not wired yet) ---
# SIM-40 deferred enabling Turnstile until the FE renders the widget. When that lands,
# the anon sign-in must send a captcha token (see setCaptchaTokenProvider in
# stores/auth.store.ts). The SITE key is public; the SECRET key goes in Supabase only.
# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
